   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Ml Exercise Guide",
   "text": "Assignment 2: Choosing a Metric\nTask. A fraud detection dataset has 1% fraudulent transactions. A teammate reports 99% accuracy. Decide whether the model is good.\nExpected answer. Accuracy is not informative here because a model that predicts \"not fraud\" for everything also reaches 99%. Evaluate precision, recall, F1 and the precision-recall curve. In fraud detection, missing a fraud (a false negative) is usually costly, so recall is emphasized, while precision controls how many legitimate customers are inconvenienced.",
